---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro';

const toc = [
  { id: 'status', text: 'Status' },
  { id: 'api-first', text: 'Use the REST API now' },
];
---

<Docs
  title="MCP integration"
  description="MCP support is planned after the first REST API capabilities are in place."
  toc={toc}
  updated="October 2026"
>
  <h2 id="status">Status</h2>
  <Callout type="note" title="Not available yet">
    The x-web MCP server and remote MCP endpoint are not implemented. We are building and validating
    the search API first; MCP can be added as a client adapter after that contract is stable.
  </Callout>
  <p>
    No package named <code>x-web-mcp</code>, hosted MCP URL, or account-issued x-web API key is
    required or available today. Avoid using the example configs you may see in older drafts of
    these docs.
  </p>

  <h2 id="api-first">Use the REST API now</h2>
  <p>
    Your agent can call <code>POST /api/v1/search</code> from a server-side tool/function and pass
    the returned answer, citations and results to the model. See the
    <a href="/docs/quickstart">quickstart</a> for working cURL and JavaScript examples.
  </p>
</Docs>
